    "riskScenarios": [{"id":"hallucination","likelihood":3,"impact":4,"timeHorizon":3,"notes":"The support-drafting tool could produce a confident but wrong answer. The risk is contained because drafts require human approval before sending."},{"id":"credential","likelihood":3,"impact":5,"timeHorizon":3,"notes":"Twelve AI tools and several integrations run on personal keys or over-broad scopes. A compromised key could reach ERP and CRM data."},{"id":"cascade","likelihood":4,"impact":4,"timeHorizon":3,"notes":"Quoting, scheduling, and procurement all depend on the order sync and the price book. A failure in either ripples across all three."},{"id":"dataQuality","likelihood":4,"impact":4,"timeHorizon":4,"notes":"Pricing exists in three conflicting versions and the quality DB is ungoverned. AI built on this would learn the errors."},{"id":"ceiling","likelihood":5,"impact":4,"timeHorizon":4,"notes":"The sub-1-day quoting goal needs clean customer and pricing data, a quoting-to-ERP integration, and inference compute. None of it fully exists yet."}],
    "dataGovernance": {"cadence":"Monthly","authority":"Sets data-quality standards per domain, assigns domain owners, approves new data sources for AI use, and can block AI initiatives that depend on ungoverned data.","escalation":"Cross-domain disputes escalate to the COO. Data-privacy questions escalate to Legal.","platform":"A governed warehouse on Azure as the single serving layer for analytics and AI, with the data lake holding raw and curated extracts beneath it. Microsoft Purview, rolling out now, catalogs every source and traces lineage. Quality rules run in dbt on the warehouse. Systems of record stay where they are and feed the warehouse; the shared drives and the Access database are consolidated into it over the next two quarters.","residency":"Customer and production data stay in US regions. Nothing leaves North America. Vendor contracts name the storage region.","domains":[{"name":"Customer & Account","owner":"Sales Ops Lead","qualityThreshold":"Gold","standards":"Deduplicated accounts, validated addresses, a single source of truth in Salesforce. Under 2% duplicates."},{"name":"Product & Pricing","owner":"Product Manager","qualityThreshold":"Gold","standards":"One authoritative, versioned price book. No spreadsheet overrides permitted for quoting."},{"name":"Production & Quality","owner":"Plant Engineering Lead","qualityThreshold":"Silver","standards":"Line QA measurements migrated off Access into the warehouse, with field-level validation and a daily backup."},{"name":"Supplier & Procurement","owner":"Procurement Manager","qualityThreshold":"Bronze","standards":"Supplier master cleaned and lead-times captured. Not yet AI-ready."}],"forumMembers":[{"id":"f1","name":"Harriet Rivers","title":"COO","role":"Chair","parent":""},{"id":"f2","name":"Shalini Mehta","title":"Head of Data","role":"Member","parent":"f1"},{"id":"f3","name":"Vincent Lau","title":"VP Engineering","role":"Member","parent":"f1"},{"id":"f4","name":"Ray Caruso","title":"Security Lead","role":"Member","parent":"f3"},{"id":"f5","name":"Duncan Fairley","title":"Plant Systems Lead","role":"Member","parent":"f3"},{"id":"f6","name":"Freya Lindqvist","title":"Enterprise Architect","role":"Member","parent":"f3"}],"blockersList":["Pricing data lives in three conflicting versions","The Access quality DB has never been backed up","No agreed definition of an “active customer” across CRM and ERP"],"consolidationList":["Migrate the Access quality DB into the governed warehouse","Collapse three pricing spreadsheets into one versioned price book","Retire the duplicate marketing-contact store in HubSpot"],"reviewLog":[{"at":T(-4685400000),"by":"Harriet Rivers, COO","findings":{"domains":4,"unowned":0,"systems":8,"notGoverned":6,"failing":4,"noPlan":0,"late":0,"below":4,"unassessed":2,"newSystems":8,"consolidation":3,"blockers":3,"sovMet":1,"sovTotal":6,"sovActions":1,"platform":true},"agenda":["Data Domains: Check that the data domain list covers all appropriate areas and that every domain has a named owner. Review any data domain added since the last meeting.","Data Platform: Review your platform strategy, consolidation priorities, blockers, and dependencies, and make changes where needed.","New Data Systems: Review every data system added to the map since the last meeting and confirm it has been assessed.","Data Quality Improvement Plans: Check that every data system that does not meet its selected standards has a data quality improvement plan with an owner and a target date. Check which plans are past their target date and decide what happens to each. Confirm which plans are complete and record that the system now meets its standards.","Decisions and Report: Record what the review decided, with owners and dates. Log the review. The log is the report the Architecture Review Board reads."],"notes":"All four domains have named owners. Six of the eight data systems are not yet formally governed, the sales mart and the Access quality database among them; the four systems that do not meet their standards each carry an improvement plan with an owner and a date, and none is past its target. The two systems the plants adopted on their own have not yet been assessed. Consolidation onto the governed warehouse is on track, with the Access migration the one blocker.","decisions":[{"id":"dgd1","text":"Bring the sales mart under the forum’s standards, with the Sales Ops Lead as its owner","owner":"Shalini Mehta","date":D(-5)},{"id":"dgd2","text":"Assess the two plant-adopted systems against the Silver standard before the next meeting","owner":"Duncan Fairley","date":D(-23)},{"id":"dgd3","text":"Hold the Access quality database to its December retirement and report progress at each meeting","owner":"IT Manager","date":D(71)}]}],"review":{"walk":{},"decisions":[],"decSeq":3}},
    "apiPolicy": {"default":"API-first is the default for every new connection. Anything that cannot go through the managed gateway needs a written exception.","exceptions":"Exceptions go to the Architecture Review Board with the reason and a retirement date for the workaround.","owner":"Vincent Lau, VP Engineering"},
